===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm-nor|walde}}, from {{inh|en|ang|wealdan||to rule, control, determine, direct, command, govern, possess, wield, exercise, cause, bring about}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*waldan}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*waldaną||to reign}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*waldʰ-||to be strong, be powerful, prevail, possess}}.

{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|de|walten||to prevail, reign, dominate}}, {{cog|da|-}} {{m|sv|volde||to cause}}, {{cog|is|valda||to cause}}, {{cog|lt|valda||land property}}, {{cog|lt|valdyti||to rule}}.
{{col-bottom}}

====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|UK|_|dialectal|ambitransitive}} To [[govern]]; [[inherit]].

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm-nor|wald}}, from {{inh|en|ang|weald||power, authority}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*waldą||power}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*waldʰ-||to be strong, be powerful, prevail, possess}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|Gewalt||force, power, control, violence}}, {{cog|sv|våld||force, violence}}.

