From {{inh|en|enm-nor|wald}}, from {{inh|en|ang|weald||high land covered with wood, woods, forest}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*walþu}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*walþuz}}, whence also Old High German {{m|goh|wald}} (German {{m|de|Wald}}) and Old Norse {{m|non|vǫllr}} (Faroese {{m|fo|vøllur}}, Norwegian {{m|no|voll}}, Icelandic {{m|is|völlur}}).

